4
00:00:18,457 --> 00:00:21,127
(Lee Sung Hoon and Go Seok Hyun)

5
00:00:21,127 --> 00:00:24,297
(Kim Kwan Hoon and Kim Ho Yoon)

6
00:00:24,397 --> 00:00:27,367
(Lee Yeon Bok and Kim Min Seong)

7
00:00:27,367 --> 00:00:30,307
(Jung Ho Young and Hong Seok Cheon)

8
00:00:30,307 --> 00:00:33,307
(Kim Mi Ryeong and Edward Kwon)

9
00:00:33,307 --> 00:00:36,677
(Choi Sang Hyun and Kim Hoon)

10
00:00:36,817 --> 00:00:39,647
This round will be a blind competition.

11
00:00:39,647 --> 00:00:40,717
(A blind team mission)

12
00:00:40,717 --> 00:00:42,787
(They can attract customers when wearing mascot costumes.)

13
00:00:43,957 --> 00:00:45,317
Each alliance team must...

14
00:00:45,617 --> 00:00:48,857
choose 2 out of 4 available dishes.

15
00:00:48,857 --> 00:00:50,127
(100 serving relay team match)

16
00:00:50,127 --> 00:00:53,527
The two selected dishes will be sold in a relay format.

17
00:00:53,527 --> 00:00:54,697
(Dish for the 1st half, dish for the 2nd half)

18
00:00:54,927 --> 00:00:56,667
The starting team must...

19
00:00:56,667 --> 00:00:58,867
sell 50 bowls before...

20
00:00:58,867 --> 00:01:01,867
the following team can begin selling.

21
00:01:02,307 --> 00:01:04,977
Including 50 bowls of the following team,

22
00:01:04,977 --> 00:01:08,507
the 1st 2 restaurants to sell a total of 100 bowls will...

23
00:01:09,347 --> 00:01:11,517
advance to the next round.

24
00:01:11,517 --> 00:01:14,247
(Only the 1st 2 alliance teams to sell 100 dishes will survive.)

25
00:01:14,387 --> 00:01:17,157
(Including a beverage, each dish is sold for 13 dollars.)

26
00:01:17,357 --> 00:01:18,357
However...

27
00:01:18,387 --> 00:01:19,727
Is it not ready yet?

28
00:01:19,727 --> 00:01:22,687
(If a customer complaint occurs)

29
00:01:22,687 --> 00:01:24,727
One additional dish as a penalty.

30
00:01:24,727 --> 00:01:27,567
(For 2 points of customer ratings,)

31
00:01:27,567 --> 00:01:28,967
(1 additional dish is added.)

32
00:01:28,967 --> 00:01:31,167
(For 1 point of customer ratings,)

33
00:01:31,567 --> 00:01:33,267
(2 additional dishes are added.)

34
00:01:33,267 --> 00:01:37,637
(They must sell all penalty bowls to survive.)

35
00:01:37,637 --> 00:01:40,807
(100 serving relay team match starts.)

36
00:01:41,447 --> 00:01:44,247
(Kim Mi Ryeong and Edward Kwon's Aunties Kitchen)

37
00:01:44,317 --> 00:01:45,517
We're the starting team.

38
00:01:45,517 --> 00:01:46,587
(Kim Mi Ryeong in charge of the first half menu)

39
00:01:46,587 --> 00:01:48,247
It has a variety of flavours,

40
00:01:48,247 --> 00:01:50,287
so I thought the customers would like it.

41
00:01:51,117 --> 00:01:52,617
We have five orders.

42
00:01:52,917 --> 00:01:54,587
We just got a new one, so we have six.

43
00:01:54,887 --> 00:01:55,927
Okay.

44
00:01:57,057 --> 00:01:59,257
(Corn cheese)

45
00:01:59,257 --> 00:02:01,027
The cheese got too hard.

46
00:02:03,397 --> 00:02:05,097
The cheese got too hard.

47
00:02:08,537 --> 00:02:10,207
Hold on. Let's see.

48
00:02:12,637 --> 00:02:15,307
This is too thick.

49
00:02:18,517 --> 00:02:21,447
We were short on time...

50
00:02:21,447 --> 00:02:23,757
and had to prepare a large quantity,

51
00:02:23,817 --> 00:02:27,227
so we made a lot of the corn cheese in advance.

52
00:02:27,657 --> 00:02:30,397
But the cheese completely hardened.

53
00:02:34,967 --> 00:02:36,027
Wait a minute.

54
00:02:38,067 --> 00:02:39,197
(Glancing cautiously)

55
00:02:39,537 --> 00:02:41,737
Seok Su, get the wok on the stove.

56
00:02:44,577 --> 00:02:47,147
(Getting the wok ready)

57
00:02:47,647 --> 00:02:49,147
Pour two cartons of heavy cream for me.

58
00:02:49,747 --> 00:02:51,177
Okay.

59
00:02:51,677 --> 00:02:54,117
We're on the same team.

60
00:02:54,117 --> 00:02:55,717
As a senior in the industry,

61
00:02:55,717 --> 00:02:58,987
the right thing to do was to step in and help them out.

62
00:02:59,317 --> 00:03:00,457
We're going to reduce it.

63
00:03:00,457 --> 00:03:03,257
When making cream pasta, you reduce the cream.

64
00:03:03,257 --> 00:03:06,127
I had to reduce it and get the right consistency.

65
00:03:07,667 --> 00:03:09,697
- The cheese must be melted.
- Okay.

66
00:03:13,537 --> 00:03:15,007
I was incredibly grateful,

67
00:03:15,007 --> 00:03:17,137
but I felt bad about it.

68
00:03:17,907 --> 00:03:18,977
It was our dish,

69
00:03:19,237 --> 00:03:20,507
yet they were fixing it for us.

70
00:03:21,807 --> 00:03:24,117
(Jun Seong is frozen with guilt over his mistake.)

71
00:03:24,217 --> 00:03:26,417
- We have another order.
- Okay.

72
00:03:26,747 --> 00:03:27,987
We have another one.

73
00:03:29,687 --> 00:03:32,117
(Orders are piling up with nothing going out.)

74
00:03:32,487 --> 00:03:34,257
Gosh, the cheese isn't melting.

75
00:03:36,157 --> 00:03:38,927
(The cheese shows no signs of melting.)

76
00:03:38,927 --> 00:03:40,697
Let me see. Lift it.

77
00:03:40,697 --> 00:03:43,097
No, it's a mess. There's no way to fix it.

78
00:03:43,367 --> 00:03:44,637
Let's put a bowl...

79
00:03:44,867 --> 00:03:47,107
or something underneath it and strain it.

80
00:03:49,207 --> 00:03:50,577
(Preparing the strainer)

81
00:03:50,577 --> 00:03:51,637
Move out of the way.

82
00:03:51,677 --> 00:03:53,347
I figured it was best to keep...

83
00:03:53,347 --> 00:03:56,477
the sauce that had absorbed the corn flavour...

84
00:03:56,777 --> 00:04:00,417
and quickly remove clumps of cheese.

85
00:04:01,347 --> 00:04:02,417
Is it okay now?

86
00:04:03,287 --> 00:04:06,927
We reheated the sauce mixed with the heavy cream.

87
00:04:07,357 --> 00:04:09,157
Do we have more corn?

88
00:04:09,157 --> 00:04:10,857
- Yes, we have canned corn.
- Can you add one can?

89
00:04:11,257 --> 00:04:13,697
Then we added more corn...

90
00:04:13,697 --> 00:04:15,327
to increase the quantity.

91
00:04:15,327 --> 00:04:18,437
It was essentially a creamy corn sauce.

92
00:04:19,397 --> 00:04:20,867
About this much?

93
00:04:20,867 --> 00:04:22,907
(Adding more salt for seasoning)

94
00:04:22,907 --> 00:04:24,977
I have some cheese over there.

95
00:04:26,037 --> 00:04:27,347
I'll give you this cheese.

96
00:04:27,347 --> 00:04:28,577
- Sprinkle some on top.
- Okay.

97
00:04:28,577 --> 00:04:29,917
- Okay, you got it now?
- Yes.

98
00:04:29,917 --> 00:04:32,147
At the temperature the dish will be served,

99
00:04:32,147 --> 00:04:34,387
the cheese should be warm enough to melt...

100
00:04:34,487 --> 00:04:35,547
when mixed in.

101
00:04:35,617 --> 00:04:38,217
So we decided to add the cheese at the end.

102
00:04:38,787 --> 00:04:40,027
- You understand it now, right?
- Yes.

103
00:04:40,027 --> 00:04:41,427
Okay, let's go.

104
00:04:41,557 --> 00:04:42,587
Let's do this.

105
00:04:43,997 --> 00:04:45,127
Do we plate it like that?

106
00:04:45,127 --> 00:04:46,127
(Spreading the sweet potato mousse...)

107
00:04:46,127 --> 00:04:48,597
(and topping it with corn cheese)

108
00:04:48,927 --> 00:04:51,437
(Sprinkling the cheese on top before serving)

109
00:04:56,037 --> 00:04:57,737
Currently, we have 13 orders.

110
00:04:58,007 --> 00:04:59,537
- Okay.
- Thirteen orders?

111
00:04:59,577 --> 00:05:00,907
Yes, we have 13 orders.

112
00:05:01,047 --> 00:05:02,107
Clear this area...

113
00:05:02,107 --> 00:05:03,417
- and prepare 13 dishes here.
- Okay.

114
00:05:03,417 --> 00:05:04,617
We'll send them out all in one go.

115
00:05:04,877 --> 00:05:08,217
I don't know if I could call it taking the lead,

116
00:05:08,487 --> 00:05:10,017
but I felt that...

117
00:05:10,017 --> 00:05:12,217
establishing a system quickly was important.

118
00:05:12,487 --> 00:05:13,857
Clear this area first.

119
00:05:13,857 --> 00:05:15,027
Is that corn?

120
00:05:15,157 --> 00:05:16,527
- Yes.
- Put the corn here.

121
00:05:17,057 --> 00:05:18,357
I'll cut the gimbap here.

122
00:05:18,357 --> 00:05:20,597
Yes, just keep cutting them.

123
00:05:21,097 --> 00:05:23,367
I'll put the salad with the sauce and serve it.

124
00:05:23,497 --> 00:05:24,997
He told us what needed to be done first.

125
00:05:25,267 --> 00:05:28,107
Thanks to him, we were off to a smooth start.

126
00:05:32,037 --> 00:05:33,277
He was amazing.

127
00:05:33,777 --> 00:05:36,077
As expected, he knew what he was doing.

128
00:05:37,017 --> 00:05:40,217
For a team that hasn't worked together to find its rhythm,

129
00:05:40,217 --> 00:05:42,087
someone has to step up...

130
00:05:42,147 --> 00:05:43,147
- And lead the way.
- and lead the way.

131
00:05:43,147 --> 00:05:44,387
Edward did it...

132
00:05:44,517 --> 00:05:46,117
very well.

133
00:05:46,317 --> 00:05:47,687
So everything came together more smoothly.

134
00:05:48,687 --> 00:05:50,627
Is it done? This one is ready.

135
00:05:50,627 --> 00:05:52,027
(Food being plated quickly)

136
00:05:52,557 --> 00:05:53,727
Enjoy your food.

137
00:05:53,897 --> 00:05:54,997
Enjoy your food.

138
00:05:55,797 --> 00:05:56,867
Enjoy your food.

139
00:05:58,167 --> 00:06:00,367
- Most of our orders are out.
- Okay.

140
00:06:01,707 --> 00:06:03,267
(Number of orders after 20 minutes)

141
00:06:03,267 --> 00:06:05,837
(3rd place: Kim Mi Ryeong and Edward Kwon, 19 dishes)

142
00:06:06,377 --> 00:06:07,447
Look at the sign.

143
00:06:07,747 --> 00:06:09,247
Isn't Chap Chap Chu popular?

144
00:06:09,247 --> 00:06:10,247
It is.

145
00:06:10,347 --> 00:06:13,017
(Chap Chu, Chap Chu, Chap Chap Chu)

146
00:06:13,247 --> 00:06:14,517
(Crazy Flavour Restaurant)

147
00:06:14,517 --> 00:06:16,317
- It's Chap Chap Chu.
- Chap Chap Chu.

148
00:06:16,887 --> 00:06:18,087
Customer ratings are important.

149
00:06:19,017 --> 00:06:20,927
We fought hard to make it back here. We can't lose.

150
00:06:21,627 --> 00:06:22,887
Our two teams have been...

151
00:06:22,887 --> 00:06:24,657
strong candidates for elimination...

152
00:06:24,657 --> 00:06:26,527
in every mission so far.

153
00:06:27,097 --> 00:06:28,897
Naturally, no one sees us as a threat.

154
00:06:30,897 --> 00:06:33,467
(During the restaurant ledger inspections)

155
00:06:33,967 --> 00:06:36,637
(Starting with Kids Restaurant,)

156
00:06:36,637 --> 00:06:39,737
(other restaurants were being inspected.)

157
00:06:40,577 --> 00:06:41,607
Is there no one?

158
00:06:41,607 --> 00:06:42,677
(Crazy Flavour Restaurant)

159
00:06:42,807 --> 00:06:44,377
Why isn't anyone checking us?

160
00:06:46,447 --> 00:06:47,647
I thought,

161
00:06:47,847 --> 00:06:50,517
"They don't care what we do."

162
00:06:50,787 --> 00:06:53,487
Dying once is hard enough. What's hard about dying twice?

163
00:06:53,487 --> 00:06:57,157
We wanted to show them how immortal we were.

164
00:06:57,597 --> 00:06:58,827
We'll keep surviving.

165
00:06:58,827 --> 00:06:59,897
(Surviving team from revival match, Kim Kwan Hoon and Kim Ho Yoon)

166
00:07:00,397 --> 00:07:02,967
Feel free to tell us your ideas.

167
00:07:03,097 --> 00:07:04,297
- Our restaurant name...
- Our name...

168
00:07:04,797 --> 00:07:06,667
When it comes to naming something,

169
00:07:06,737 --> 00:07:08,207
it's easier when one person makes...

170
00:07:08,207 --> 00:07:10,777
a suggestion and everyone else agrees.

171
00:07:11,707 --> 00:07:13,307
We'll think about it.

172
00:07:13,307 --> 00:07:15,947
We'll think of something catchy.

173
00:07:16,307 --> 00:07:18,077
After a lot of intense thinking,

174
00:07:18,077 --> 00:07:20,687
we decided on a Gen Z concept...

175
00:07:21,017 --> 00:07:23,617
aimed at middle and high school students.

176
00:07:24,387 --> 00:07:25,717
We named it Crazy Flavour Restaurant.

177
00:07:27,987 --> 00:07:31,627
"Chap Chap Chu" is a trendy and catchy expression...

178
00:07:31,857 --> 00:07:35,267
for describing something delicious.

179
00:07:35,827 --> 00:07:38,437
It was a funny and witty concept...

180
00:07:38,767 --> 00:07:41,107
that we could use for the restaurant's sign and promotion.

181
00:07:41,107 --> 00:07:42,407
(Crazy Flavour Restaurant)

182
00:07:42,967 --> 00:07:44,377
Hello, puppy.

183
00:07:44,537 --> 00:07:46,477
(Hello, it's this way.)

184
00:07:46,777 --> 00:07:47,777
I was born...

185
00:07:47,947 --> 00:07:50,447
in 1979, and I turned 48 this year.

186
00:07:50,577 --> 00:07:51,917
It was my first time wearing a mascot costume.

187
00:07:58,987 --> 00:08:00,017
I can't see anything.

188
00:08:00,857 --> 00:08:01,927
The eyes are too far away.

189
00:08:02,757 --> 00:08:04,697
The eyes were over here like this.

190
00:08:05,097 --> 00:08:07,197
I could barely see anything.

191
00:08:08,367 --> 00:08:10,167
Gosh, I stepped on a camera.

192
00:08:10,937 --> 00:08:12,437
(A dog with a limited field of vision)

193
00:08:13,537 --> 00:08:15,267
I'm stepping on all the cameras.

194
00:08:16,137 --> 00:08:19,077
(Greeting customers with a narrow field of view)

195
00:08:19,137 --> 00:08:21,047
(He drops his glove.)

196
00:08:24,177 --> 00:08:25,617
Please help me find my glove.

197
00:08:25,977 --> 00:08:27,787
(A customer helps him.)

198
00:08:28,247 --> 00:08:30,987
(The mascot costume promotion is hard for the 48-year-old.)

199
00:08:32,587 --> 00:08:33,627
Thank you.

200
00:08:35,027 --> 00:08:37,897
I took on that role, so I wanted to give it a shot.

201
00:08:37,897 --> 00:08:40,097
Trying something new can be fun.

202
00:08:40,497 --> 00:08:42,997
There's no reason I can't make it work.

203
00:08:43,467 --> 00:08:44,737
Do we have the sample?

204
00:08:45,467 --> 00:08:46,537
Here's the sample.

205
00:08:50,837 --> 00:08:52,277
We were the first team to start.

206
00:08:52,407 --> 00:08:54,847
The most important was choosing an item...

207
00:08:54,847 --> 00:08:56,177
that was perfectly suited to the location.

208
00:08:56,477 --> 00:08:58,417
- This could work really well.
- Right.

209
00:08:58,417 --> 00:08:59,717
I'm all for it.

210
00:09:00,387 --> 00:09:02,817
If we choose this, we could make the perfect dish for it.

211
00:09:02,817 --> 00:09:03,887
- Exactly.
- Shall we go with this?

212
00:09:04,317 --> 00:09:06,157
- Okay.
- Yes, we made our decision.

213
00:09:06,957 --> 00:09:08,727
I didn't think there would be another team...

214
00:09:08,727 --> 00:09:10,457
that uses the container better than we could.

215
00:09:10,797 --> 00:09:13,727
For the first round, our menu items are...

216
00:09:13,727 --> 00:09:17,467
bouquet fritter and honey garlic fried rice cake.

217
00:09:17,597 --> 00:09:20,607
(They're making tteokbokki again.)

218
00:09:21,207 --> 00:09:23,137
Our strategy is to make a milder...

219
00:09:23,137 --> 00:09:25,837
honey garlic sauce with plenty of condensed milk.

220
00:09:26,407 --> 00:09:28,407
It's a type of rice cake that anyone can...

221
00:09:28,407 --> 00:09:29,847
easily enjoy.

222
00:09:30,477 --> 00:09:33,277
As more of a side dish than a full meal,

223
00:09:33,347 --> 00:09:34,917
it can be enjoyed as an appetizer.

224
00:09:35,087 --> 00:09:36,817
We deliberately chose this menu item.

225
00:09:38,187 --> 00:09:39,587
It will be very delicious.

226
00:09:39,587 --> 00:09:40,757
(Sweet and crunchy honey garlic fried rice cake)

227
00:09:41,187 --> 00:09:42,527
The key to our fritter dish is...

228
00:09:42,527 --> 00:09:48,267
putting everything on skewers and arranging it like a bouquet.

229
00:09:49,427 --> 00:09:53,097
(Chicken, shrimp, squid)

230
00:09:53,097 --> 00:09:55,567
(Honey garlic fried rice cake)

231
00:09:55,567 --> 00:09:56,567
(Gochujang aioli)

232
00:09:56,567 --> 00:09:58,437
The drink sits at the bottom of the container.

233
00:09:58,777 --> 00:10:02,347
The food spreads upward and gives it a lot of height.

234
00:10:02,807 --> 00:10:05,017
When someone is carrying it with one hand or both,

235
00:10:05,447 --> 00:10:06,917
people would see it and think, "Which restaurant is it from?"

236
00:10:07,247 --> 00:10:09,587
We thought the visual appeal would draw people to us.

237
00:10:09,987 --> 00:10:12,557
Gosh, let's get that. Snowflake chicken thigh.

238
00:10:13,787 --> 00:10:15,187
- That looks good.
- Which one?

239
00:10:15,287 --> 00:10:16,727
It looks like deep-fried shrimp.

240
00:10:17,857 --> 00:10:18,897
It's unusual.

241
00:10:19,427 --> 00:10:20,527
- Shall we get it?
- Okay.

242
00:10:20,997 --> 00:10:24,467
(Customers gather after seeing the sample.)

243
00:10:24,997 --> 00:10:26,667
- We have one order.
- Okay.

244
00:10:29,837 --> 00:10:31,877
(Snowflake cheese)

245
00:10:31,877 --> 00:10:34,107
When it goes out, people will be...

246
00:10:34,307 --> 00:10:36,107
impressed by it and buy it.

247
00:10:36,947 --> 00:10:39,517
(Hoping the customers themselves would promote it)

248
00:10:40,817 --> 00:10:42,587
(One person interested)

249
00:10:42,587 --> 00:10:45,217
(Another one interested)

250
00:10:45,617 --> 00:10:48,457
That bouquet fritter looks good.

251
00:10:49,087 --> 00:10:50,327
After looking at it,

252
00:10:50,897 --> 00:10:52,797
the fritter skewers look delicious.

253
00:10:54,627 --> 00:10:55,627
Make an order.

254
00:10:55,627 --> 00:10:57,237
(Thanks to the visual appeal, the waiting line gets long.)

255
00:10:57,237 --> 00:10:58,467
Shall we get one for now?

256
00:10:58,467 --> 00:10:59,497
I can't wait to try it.

257
00:10:59,937 --> 00:11:01,207
The orders are coming in like crazy.

258
00:11:01,307 --> 00:11:02,407
They'll keep coming.

259
00:11:02,867 --> 00:11:05,107
Are you frying chicken right now?

260
00:11:05,107 --> 00:11:06,377
Yes, I'm frying chicken.

261
00:11:06,607 --> 00:11:08,607
We still need ten more dishes.

262
00:11:08,607 --> 00:11:10,077
Ten? My gosh.

263
00:11:10,747 --> 00:11:13,687
A lot of orders came in all of a sudden.

264
00:11:14,247 --> 00:11:15,587
This is good.

265
00:11:16,117 --> 00:11:18,317
(Crazy Flavour Restaurant is advancing quickly.)

266
00:11:18,317 --> 00:11:19,817
Here's your order.

267
00:11:20,427 --> 00:11:22,357
Do I press call for all the incoming orders?

268
00:11:22,357 --> 00:11:23,357
Yes.

269
00:11:27,997 --> 00:11:29,997
I expect it to be a race against the clock.

270
00:11:30,597 --> 00:11:32,167
Who can sell the most the fastest.

271
00:11:32,737 --> 00:11:34,767
How many orders did we get? What number is it?

272
00:11:34,867 --> 00:11:36,107
We're at number 43.

273
00:11:36,107 --> 00:11:37,777
(Crazy Flavour Restaurant sold 7 dishes.)

274
00:11:37,777 --> 00:11:38,977
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

275
00:11:40,077 --> 00:11:42,347
