Shrimp and...

1325
00:54:25,339 --> 00:54:27,209
Do you need shrimp now?

1326
00:54:27,209 --> 00:54:28,469
We're out of shrimp.

1327
00:54:28,509 --> 00:54:30,139
- Shrimp?
- Darn it.

1328
00:54:30,679 --> 00:54:33,349
Please let me know in advance when we're running low on something.

1329
00:54:34,009 --> 00:54:36,109
Just fry everything up. We're out of everything.

1330
00:54:36,109 --> 00:54:37,179
Okay.

1331
00:54:37,519 --> 00:54:40,689
Chef Sung Hoon's cooking style...

1332
00:54:40,789 --> 00:54:42,349
felt like a master craftsman,

1333
00:54:42,349 --> 00:54:45,459
so we couldn't really rush him.

1334
00:54:46,989 --> 00:54:51,799
(Frying time per portion)

1335
00:54:51,799 --> 00:54:54,329
(3 minutes)

1336
00:54:54,699 --> 00:54:58,669
(He'd have to fry non-stop for about 2 hours to pull this off.)

1337
00:54:58,669 --> 00:55:01,309
Just keep handing over the finished dishes.

1338
00:55:01,309 --> 00:55:02,469
Okay.

1339
00:55:02,469 --> 00:55:05,079
While frying the food, I could really feel it.

1340
00:55:05,079 --> 00:55:06,949
That the orders were backing up.

1341
00:55:07,679 --> 00:55:09,179
"Come on. Hurry up with the fried food."

1342
00:55:09,779 --> 00:55:11,249
"Come on. Hurry up with the fried food."

1343
00:55:12,049 --> 00:55:16,149
Frying tendon in real time and serving it right away...

1344
00:55:16,619 --> 00:55:18,759
is not easy time-wise.

1345
00:55:19,219 --> 00:55:20,459
Did you get the call?

1346
00:55:20,459 --> 00:55:21,859
I have not received the call notification yet.

1347
00:55:21,859 --> 00:55:25,099
We are calling customers in order right now,

1348
00:55:25,099 --> 00:55:26,599
so it might take a while.

1349
00:55:26,599 --> 00:55:27,769
But it's been 30 minutes already.

1350
00:55:27,769 --> 00:55:29,029
We will have it ready shortly.

1351
00:55:29,469 --> 00:55:30,599
We will make it quick.

1352
00:55:30,599 --> 00:55:31,999
- We will get it done quickly.
- Please take it.

1353
00:55:33,809 --> 00:55:35,609
(The customers finally received the DonDon Set after a long wait.)

1354
00:55:35,609 --> 00:55:36,879
We're like food fighters now.

1355
00:55:36,879 --> 00:55:39,079
- Finally, it's Lulu Land.
- Finally.

1356
00:55:40,579 --> 00:55:41,779
- This is good.
- Yes.

1357
00:55:41,779 --> 00:55:43,719
(Humming)

1358
00:55:44,019 --> 00:55:45,879
(It is good enough to make up for the long wait.)

1359
00:55:45,879 --> 00:55:46,919
What kind of sauce is this?

1360
00:55:48,049 --> 00:55:50,919
(However)

1361
00:55:50,919 --> 00:55:53,089
The poached egg and fatsia shoots are missing.

1362
00:55:53,389 --> 00:55:54,659
This is unbelievable.

1363
00:55:56,999 --> 00:55:59,099
(Conger eel, shrimp, fatsia shoots, oyster mushroom,)

1364
00:55:59,099 --> 00:56:01,229
(squash, green chilli pepper, laver, poached egg)

1365
00:56:01,429 --> 00:56:03,339
We waited so long.

1366
00:56:03,339 --> 00:56:05,599
And they did not even give us the egg.

1367
00:56:06,269 --> 00:56:09,409
(Lulu Land)

1368
00:56:09,709 --> 00:56:13,679
Two plates are added to Lulu Land as a penalty.

1369
00:56:14,079 --> 00:56:15,149
Oh, no.

1370
00:56:15,479 --> 00:56:17,779
I think it is probably because there was a wait.

1371
00:56:17,779 --> 00:56:18,779
(The first penalty is incurred.)

1372
00:56:19,119 --> 00:56:20,389
(The udon is great, and the tendon tastes like one from a restaurant.)

1373
00:56:20,389 --> 00:56:21,589
(I like that the fried food is hot, but it takes way too long.)

1374
00:56:21,589 --> 00:56:22,919
(This is no ordinary tendon. I enjoyed the meal.)

1375
00:56:22,919 --> 00:56:28,189
(Despite positive reviews, there are many complaints about the wait.)

1376
00:56:28,489 --> 00:56:29,629
It's all right, Chef.

1377
00:56:31,429 --> 00:56:33,169
"Everyone is doing their best right now,"

1378
00:56:33,569 --> 00:56:35,469
"but how much time do we have left?"

1379
00:56:35,999 --> 00:56:38,499
I was feeling very anxious, but I didn't want to show it.

1380
00:56:38,499 --> 00:56:39,869
I didn't want to waver.

1381
00:56:40,069 --> 00:56:41,369
(Lee Sung Hoon and Go Seok Hyun)

1382
00:56:41,369 --> 00:56:44,809
Let us all focus on right here...

1383
00:56:44,979 --> 00:56:46,849
- until we sell all these dishes.
- Okay.

1384
00:56:48,479 --> 00:56:49,649
It's all right.

1385
00:56:50,149 --> 00:56:51,649
It's okay. We only need to take second place.

1386
00:56:52,949 --> 00:56:54,789
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1387
00:56:54,789 --> 00:56:55,919
Enjoy your food.

1388
00:56:55,919 --> 00:56:59,089
- Enjoy your food.
- Thank you. I'll enjoy the food.

1389
00:56:59,559 --> 00:57:00,959
We have only two left.

1390
00:57:01,129 --> 00:57:02,659
- Fry two servings?
- Yes.

1391
00:57:03,499 --> 00:57:05,329
- Then we're done?
- Yes.

1392
00:57:06,569 --> 00:57:07,699
Thank you.

1393
00:57:07,699 --> 00:57:08,699
(The last dish of the first half is served to the customer.)

1394
00:57:08,699 --> 00:57:09,869
Thank you.

1395
00:57:10,669 --> 00:57:14,039
Lulu Land has sold 50 plates.

1396
00:57:14,039 --> 00:57:15,639
(Clear time)

1397
00:57:15,639 --> 00:57:17,539
(Lee Yeon Bok and Kim Min Seong: 70 minutes)

1398
00:57:17,539 --> 00:57:19,379
(Lee Sung Hoon and Go Seok Hyun: 97 minutes)

1399
00:57:19,379 --> 00:57:21,879
Please open the second box.

1400
00:57:22,079 --> 00:57:23,479
I felt so rushed.

1401
00:57:23,479 --> 00:57:26,219
We finished the first half in last place.

1402
00:57:26,219 --> 00:57:27,949
So we were running out of time.

1403
00:57:27,949 --> 00:57:30,659
My hands were shaking as I unlocked the padlock.

1404
00:57:31,319 --> 00:57:33,759
(They start the 2nd half in last place after being in 1st.)

1405
00:57:35,059 --> 00:57:37,629
(About to smash the box)

1406
00:57:37,659 --> 00:57:39,629
(The 1st chef: Lee Sung Hoon)

1407
00:57:39,629 --> 00:57:40,699
(Sold out)

1408
00:57:40,699 --> 00:57:42,569
(The 2nd chef: Go Seok Hyun)

1409
00:57:42,829 --> 00:57:44,699
Please slice it now.

1410
00:57:44,899 --> 00:57:46,269
- I'll slice it.
- Okay.

1411
00:57:47,209 --> 00:57:51,239
The name of our menu item is full-topping futomaki.

1412
00:57:51,509 --> 00:57:53,309
Do you have any preferred container?

1413
00:57:53,309 --> 00:57:55,279
I personally like long ones like this.

1414
00:57:55,279 --> 00:57:56,309
Something simple.

1415
00:57:56,309 --> 00:57:57,549
(Go Seok Hyun chose the rectangular tray for the second half.)

1416
00:57:57,549 --> 00:58:00,149
I thought it should look cute.

1417
00:58:00,149 --> 00:58:01,419
So I made...

1418
00:58:01,419 --> 00:58:03,589
an animated character using a hole puncher.

1419
00:58:03,589 --> 00:58:05,019
(Adding cuteness to target children)

1420
00:58:05,019 --> 00:58:08,429
I made quail egg sunny-side-ups to put on top.

1421
00:58:08,429 --> 00:58:09,629
(Adding cute mini fried eggs)

1422
00:58:10,029 --> 00:58:13,299
(Planning to place it on top of the futomaki)

1423
00:58:13,429 --> 00:58:15,899
I thought there might be young kids too.

1424
00:58:16,069 --> 00:58:17,869
- It contains no raw ingredients.
- It's good.

1425
00:58:17,869 --> 00:58:20,569
- It usually has things like salmon.
- I see. No raw ingredients?

1426
00:58:20,569 --> 00:58:23,379
Parents would be reluctant to buy raw food for their kids.

1427
00:58:23,379 --> 00:58:24,479
So I made...

1428
00:58:24,639 --> 00:58:26,039
beef futomaki...

1429
00:58:26,909 --> 00:58:27,909
and egg futomaki.

1430
00:58:28,649 --> 00:58:30,449
I thought it would be made in big pieces,

1431
00:58:30,449 --> 00:58:33,179
but it was made rather delicate and pretty.

1432
00:58:33,179 --> 00:58:35,649
And I added delicious toppings on it.

1433
00:58:36,219 --> 00:58:40,059
The concept was for various flavours to burst in the mouth...

1434
00:58:40,059 --> 00:58:41,359
from the very first bite.

1435
00:58:41,759 --> 00:58:43,089
We need to catch up.

1436
00:58:43,089 --> 00:58:44,729
No orders have come in yet.

1437
00:58:45,959 --> 00:58:47,699
- I'll slice it first for now.
- Okay.

1438
00:58:47,699 --> 00:58:49,169
But no orders are coming in yet.

1439
00:58:49,669 --> 00:58:51,369
We didn't get any orders yet.

1440
00:58:55,469 --> 00:58:56,609
Should we try this?

1441
00:58:58,779 --> 00:59:00,849
- It has cucumber in it.
- Gosh.

1442
00:59:02,379 --> 00:59:04,149
No, it is already made.

1443
00:59:09,019 --> 00:59:11,019
Is it possible to get the futomaki without cucumber?

1444
00:59:11,259 --> 00:59:12,719
I do not think we can make it without cucumber.

1445
00:59:12,719 --> 00:59:14,129
- Okay.
- I am sorry.

1446
00:59:15,289 --> 00:59:17,399
- We can make it without cucumber.
- We will leave out cucumber.

1447
00:59:17,399 --> 00:59:18,459
We can do it without cucumber.

1448
00:59:18,459 --> 00:59:19,929
- We will make it right away.
- We can do that.

1449
00:59:20,269 --> 00:59:21,969
- Will you make one for us?
- Yes. We'll make it right away.

1450
00:59:21,969 --> 00:59:23,999
- Please place your order.
- Okay. Thank you.

1451
00:59:24,369 --> 00:59:26,709
It was so terrifying when the chefs stared at me.

1452
00:59:26,709 --> 00:59:27,909
(Laughing)

1453
00:59:27,909 --> 00:59:29,139
Now is not the time to be picky about orders.

1454
00:59:30,479 --> 00:59:32,639
- Make one without cucumber.
- Okay.

1455
00:59:32,639 --> 00:59:33,809
(Every single customer is precious.)

1456
00:59:33,809 --> 00:59:35,149
- This is the one without cucumber.
- Okay.

1457
00:59:35,709 --> 00:59:37,419
Please wait just one minute.

1458
00:59:39,679 --> 00:59:41,049
- Without cucumber?
- Yes.

1459
00:59:41,389 --> 00:59:42,989
This is the futomaki with no cucumber.

1460
00:59:43,519 --> 00:59:44,919
- Thank you. I'll enjoy it.
- It doesn't have cucumber in it.

1461
00:59:44,919 --> 00:59:46,259
Okay. Thank you.

1462
00:59:46,319 --> 00:59:47,459
Please enjoy it.

1463
00:59:47,859 --> 00:59:49,659
Let us just get some momentum going.

1464
00:59:55,629 --> 00:59:56,969
We have to catch up.

1465
01:00:00,509 --> 01:00:03,779
(Solemnly throwing off the apron)

1466
01:00:05,779 --> 01:00:08,979
(Putting on cuteness)

1467
01:00:12,849 --> 01:00:14,989
(Lulu is unsealed.)

1468
01:00:14,989 --> 01:00:18,059
- The hamster is coming out.
- Hamster?

1469
01:00:18,289 --> 01:00:20,229
The hamster is here.

1470
01:00:20,489 --> 01:00:22,659
It's the hamster!

1471
01:00:23,529 --> 01:00:24,929
Hi, hamster.

1472
01:00:24,929 --> 01:00:26,629
(Hello)

1473
01:00:27,929 --> 01:00:28,969
What's that?

1474
01:00:28,969 --> 01:00:30,799
(Gourmet toppings to put on top of futomaki)

1475
01:00:31,169 --> 01:00:35,539
"On top of the futomaki..."

1476
01:00:35,539 --> 01:00:37,309
(What will be the fate of Lee Sung Hoon and Go Seok Hyun?)

1477
01:00:37,879 --> 01:00:40,379
(Currently at the amusement park...)

1478
01:00:40,379 --> 01:00:42,079
(Kids Restaurant and Crazy Flavour Restaurant)

1479
01:00:42,079 --> 01:00:43,749
Did you get the ice cream ready?

1480
01:00:44,519 --> 01:00:47,019
- Shall we get ice cream now?
- I will scoop the ice cream now.

1481
01:00:47,019 --> 01:00:48,089
Okay.

1482
01:00:48,719 --> 01:00:49,719
(The first restaurant)

1483
01:00:49,719 --> 01:00:50,819
The second.

1484
01:00:51,759 --> 01:00:52,859
We're in second place.

1485
01:00:52,859 --> 01:00:53,859
(2nd place in the 1st half, Kim Kwan Hoon and Kim Ho Yoon)

1486
01:00:53,859 --> 01:00:55,059
We came up from last place to second place now.

1487
01:00:55,259 --> 01:00:56,289
I know.

1488
01:00:58,059 --> 01:01:01,369
(What is the second half menu of Kim Kwan Hoon and Kim Ho Yoon?)

1489
01:01:02,799 --> 01:01:04,539
(Dubai chewy bouncy mianbao xia)

1490
01:01:04,539 --> 01:01:06,839
Puppy, take orders for mianbao xia.

1491
01:01:07,239 --> 01:01:09,009
- DCB mianbao xia.
- Gosh, there's a puppy.

1492
01:01:09,739 --> 01:01:11,909
- Their menu changed to mianbao xia.
- Yes.

1493
01:01:11,909 --> 01:01:13,909
What is Dubai chewy bouncy mianbao xia?

1494
01:01:14,349 --> 01:01:16,249
Dubai chewy bouncy mianbao xia...

1495
01:01:16,249 --> 01:01:18,449
with real lemon yogurt gelato is only 13 dollars.

1496
01:01:18,679 --> 01:01:20,349
- It sounds good.
- Shall we try one?

1497
01:01:22,549 --> 01:01:26,359
For the second half, Crazy Flavour Restaurant prepared...

1498
01:01:26,359 --> 01:01:29,189
something that works as both a snack and a dessert.

1499
01:01:29,629 --> 01:01:32,229
We served DCB mianbao xia...

1500
01:01:32,229 --> 01:01:34,069
and lemon yogurt gelato in the rectangular tray.

1501
01:01:35,029 --> 01:01:37,899
We took inspiration from Dubai chewy cookies.

1502
01:01:38,469 --> 01:01:40,769
We used squid ink bread.

1503
01:01:40,769 --> 01:01:41,969
(Squid ink bread instead of cacao powder)

1504
01:01:42,339 --> 01:01:43,939
Instead of crispy kataifi,

1505
01:01:45,139 --> 01:01:47,249
we fried spring roll pastry in butter to put inside.

1506
01:01:47,809 --> 01:01:51,049
Then we added tapioca pearls to bring out the chewiness.

1507
01:01:51,249 --> 01:01:53,379
(Tapioca pearls, kataifi)

1508
01:01:54,089 --> 01:01:55,889
Bouncy shrimp balls.

1509
01:01:57,089 --> 01:02:00,759
(The filling has the characteristics of Dubai chewy cookies.)

1510
01:02:02,129 --> 01:02:04,259
Preserving all the crispiness, chewiness,

1511
01:02:04,259 --> 01:02:05,899
and bounciness.

1512
01:02:09,699 --> 01:02:12,099
The mianbao xia is easy to eat, yet packed with flavours.

1513
01:02:12,939 --> 01:02:16,879
(That's how the DCB mianbao xia is created.)

1514
01:02:17,379 --> 01:02:19,079
It is targeted at Gen Z.

1515
01:02:20,079 --> 01:02:22,979
What we intended came out quite well.

1516
01:02:24,949 --> 01:02:26,079
It looks delicious.

1517
01:02:26,349 --> 01:02:28,319
DCB mianbao xia?

1518
01:02:29,189 --> 01:02:30,589
I need to scoop the ice cream.

1519
01:02:31,789 --> 01:02:35,359
Since ice cream is preferred when the weather is hot,

1520
01:02:35,759 --> 01:02:39,199
we prepared freshly made lemon yogurt ice cream.

1521
01:02:40,869 --> 01:02:42,399
Customers need to see this texture.

1522
01:02:42,399 --> 01:02:43,569
(Handmade lemon yogurt gelato)

1523
01:02:43,699 --> 01:02:45,069
It's very chewy.

1524
01:02:46,199 --> 01:02:47,709
It is a menu item we are so confident in.

1525
01:02:48,539 --> 01:02:52,379
With the ice cream, they can settle dessert at once.

1526
01:02:53,749 --> 01:02:55,979
- This is freshly made.
- Thank you.

1527
01:02:55,979 --> 01:02:57,349
Thank you. It will be delicious.

1528
01:02:57,349 --> 01:02:58,979
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1529
01:02:58,979 --> 01:03:00,649
(Crazy Flavour Restaurant has sold 59 plates.)

1530
01:03:00,819 --> 01:03:02,519
(DCB mianbao xia and lemon yogurt gelato)

1531
01:03:02,519 --> 01:03:04,089
- Is it good?
- Yes.

1532
01:03:04,119 --> 01:03:07,629
The bread is crispy, yet it melts in your mouth.

1533
01:03:07,859 --> 01:03:10,329
- There is so much shrimp.
- I know.

1534
01:03:11,529 --> 01:03:13,629
The bread is really crispy,

1535
01:03:13,729 --> 01:03:14,899
but it does not taste oily at all.

1536
01:03:17,239 --> 01:03:18,539
It would be perfect if we only had beer.

1537
01:03:18,539 --> 01:03:19,999
It'd be perfect with beer.

1538
01:03:21,809 --> 01:03:23,539
(Despite the positive reviews, the booth is quiet.)

1539
01:03:23,539 --> 01:03:24,809
Please enjoy it.

1540
01:03:26,779 --> 01:03:28,509
(Sighing)

1541
01:03:29,609 --> 01:03:31,419
Did the customers suddenly stop coming?

1542
01:03:33,119 --> 01:03:34,719
Compared to the number of customers there,

1543
01:03:34,719 --> 01:03:36,919
I thought our ordering speed was not very fast.

1544
01:03:38,219 --> 01:03:41,259
(Unlike the hectic first half,)

1545
01:03:42,929 --> 01:03:46,429
(the second half is quiet.)

1546
01:03:46,999 --> 01:03:49,169
This is DCB mianbao xia.

1547
01:03:49,329 --> 01:03:51,099
You know I hate Dubai chewy cookies.

1548
01:03:51,969 --> 01:03:53,539
Dubai chewy bouncy mianbao xia?

1549
01:03:56,139 --> 01:03:58,939
It says Dubai chewy bouncy mianbao xia.

1550
01:03:58,939 --> 01:04:00,179
- Okay.
- Do you want to try this?

1551
01:04:00,179 --> 01:04:01,279
- No.
- You don't want it?

1552
01:04:02,479 --> 01:04:04,119
It's called "Dubai chewy."

1553
01:04:05,219 --> 01:04:06,549
I am starting to feel a bit repelled by it.

1554
01:04:07,249 --> 01:04:09,219
There are way too many similar products.

1555
01:04:09,219 --> 01:04:10,249
(Dubai chewy is a love-it-or-hate-it item.)

1556
01:04:10,489 --> 01:04:12,519
The menu item named "Dubai chewy" might have made it...

1557
01:04:12,789 --> 01:04:15,689
difficult to build sympathy with customers.

1558
01:04:15,689 --> 01:04:17,659
(Dubai chewy bouncy mianbao xia)

1559
01:04:18,399 --> 01:04:19,859
How are the other places doing? Is there a long line?

1560
01:04:21,429 --> 01:04:22,799
(The line for Kids Restaurant)

1561
01:04:22,799 --> 01:04:24,069
That line is not for us.

1562
01:04:26,469 --> 01:04:28,369
I don't know if it was because we were Crazy Flavour Restaurant,

1563
01:04:28,369 --> 01:04:30,409
but all I could see were children.

1564
01:04:31,279 --> 01:04:34,079
I felt so anxious having Kids Restaurant right next door.

1565
01:04:34,649 --> 01:04:35,779
They just do not match.

1566
01:04:35,779 --> 01:04:38,349
Crazy Flavour Restaurant and Kids Restaurant don't go well.

1567
01:04:39,019 --> 01:04:41,919
It would be weird for both of them to survive together.

1568
01:04:43,189 --> 01:04:44,659
We were targeting Gen Z.

1569
01:04:45,859 --> 01:04:48,659
I thought that one of us was not going to work out.

1570
01:04:49,359 --> 01:04:50,559
That's how I felt.

1571
01:04:50,559 --> 01:04:54,729
(What's the second half menu of Choi Sang Hyun and Kim Hoon?)

1572
01:04:55,469 --> 01:04:58,099
(Please take a look at this!)

1573
01:04:58,939 --> 01:05:01,469
(Ice cream churros and lasagna cheese balls)

1574
01:05:02,269 --> 01:05:03,409
(Kim Hoon chose the soda pop container for the second half.)

1575
01:05:03,409 --> 01:05:04,509
For the second half,

1576
01:05:04,979 --> 01:05:08,149
we prepared ice cream churros and lasagna cheese balls.

1577
01:05:09,009 --> 01:05:10,679
(The 1st chef: Choi Sang Hyun)

1578
01:05:10,679 --> 01:05:11,849
(Sold out)

1579
01:05:11,849 --> 01:05:14,019
(The 2nd chef: Kim Hoon)

1580
01:05:14,149 --> 01:05:16,919
We sold a pasta menu in the first half,

1581
01:05:16,919 --> 01:05:18,219
and for the second half,

1582
01:05:18,219 --> 01:05:20,959
we prepared a dessert with churros, ice cream, and cheese balls.

1583
01:05:21,459 --> 01:05:24,459
It's for kids, and it's what I'm most confident in.

1584
01:05:24,459 --> 01:05:25,459
(A dessert menu targeting children)

1585
01:05:25,799 --> 01:05:28,829
It is a menu item I have sold for a long time at my restaurant.

1586
01:05:29,729 --> 01:05:32,639
I have my own data showing that whenever I make lasagna,

1587
01:05:32,639 --> 01:05:34,039
I win.

1588
01:05:34,909 --> 01:05:37,039
Whenever I make lasagna, I win.

1589
01:05:37,039 --> 01:05:39,009
That's why we prepared lasagna.

1590
01:05:40,009 --> 01:05:43,049
Since the concept was set as the Kids Restaurant for kids,

1591
01:05:43,949 --> 01:05:46,319
I thought about what mothers could easily feed their children.

1592
01:05:46,849 --> 01:05:49,649
So I made the lasagna into bite-sized pieces for easy eating.

1593
01:05:50,049 --> 01:05:52,459
After boiling conchiglie pasta,

1594
01:05:52,459 --> 01:05:55,829
you stuff it with a filling made of ragu and cheese mixed together...

1595
01:05:56,129 --> 01:05:57,259
and shape it like dumplings.

1596
01:05:58,129 --> 01:05:59,929
It feels like a major holiday.

1597
01:06:00,129 --> 01:06:01,169
Is it Chuseok or something?

1598
01:06:02,269 --> 01:06:04,439
- Please fry that up quickly for me.
- Okay.

1599
01:06:04,469 --> 01:06:09,309
(Pre-frying it so the food can go out fast)

1600
01:06:10,779 --> 01:06:13,809
And what is the menu item people eat the most at an amusement park?

1601
01:06:14,279 --> 01:06:15,309
It is churros.

1602
01:06:16,479 --> 01:06:17,749
So I added churros.

1603
01:06:18,779 --> 01:06:20,549
Lasagna and churros.

1604
01:06:21,689 --> 01:06:24,789
Plus ice cream that can be eaten together on a hot day.

1605
01:06:26,019 --> 01:06:28,229
That is the ultimate three-step combo.

1606
01:06:31,099 --> 01:06:33,329
I put those three together as the ultimate weapon.

1607
01:06:33,359 --> 01:06:36,499
If I pull out this card, I will definitely win.

1608
01:06:37,239 --> 01:06:38,569
I'll win this time.

1609
01:06:38,569 --> 01:06:40,169
(Ice cream churros and lasagna cheese balls)

1610
01:06:40,669 --> 01:06:44,509
(Same dessert category, different target audience)

1611
01:06:44,739 --> 01:06:47,209
(Eagerly promoting in front of another booth)

1612
01:06:47,349 --> 01:06:51,779
(Please try the lasagna.)

1613
01:06:51,779 --> 01:06:53,949
(You get free cotton candy.)

1614
01:06:54,119 --> 01:06:55,689
It's holding up a signboard.

1615
01:06:56,019 --> 01:06:57,919
It looks like they will fight.

1616
01:07:00,359 --> 01:07:03,159
(Children are approaching, captivated by the cotton candy.)

1617
01:07:03,159 --> 01:07:04,159
Cotton candy.

1618
01:07:04,659 --> 01:07:06,129
- Cotton candy.
- Cotton candy!

1619
01:07:06,829 --> 01:07:08,369
Come. You should take it.

1620
01:07:08,369 --> 01:07:10,199
How will you get it? Do you want to try this?

1621
01:07:10,269 --> 01:07:11,269
(Nodding)

1622
01:07:12,869 --> 01:07:14,509
(Ordering)

1623
01:07:14,939 --> 01:07:16,639
I don't like lemon ice cream.

1624
01:07:17,409 --> 01:07:18,739
This isn't lemon ice cream.

1625
01:07:19,479 --> 01:07:20,479
This one?

1626
01:07:20,479 --> 01:07:22,049
(Ordering)

1627
01:07:22,979 --> 01:07:25,549
Hi, Teddy Bear!

1628
01:07:25,549 --> 01:07:26,579
(Explosive interest from children)

1629
01:07:26,919 --> 01:07:28,489
Hi, Teddy Bear!

1630
01:07:30,789 --> 01:07:34,729
(A bite of churros dipped in ice cream)

1631
01:07:35,129 --> 01:07:38,259
- This is really good.
- I want a bite!

1632
01:07:38,629 --> 01:07:40,229
- It's not a cheese stick. Try it.
- Help yourself.

1633
01:07:44,239 --> 01:07:45,299
This is really...

1634
01:07:45,499 --> 01:07:47,069
This is a lot better.

1635
01:07:47,339 --> 01:07:49,939
- The lasagna tastes good.
- It's delicious, right?

1636
01:07:50,439 --> 01:07:51,939
It's very crispy and tasty.

1637
01:07:53,439 --> 01:07:55,379
Currently, Kids Restaurant...

1638
01:07:55,909 --> 01:07:58,149
has sold 75 plates.

1639
01:07:58,149 --> 01:07:59,779
- Nice.
- Nice.

1640
01:08:00,319 --> 01:08:01,619
We finished half.

1641
01:08:02,019 --> 01:08:04,489
The kid-friendly concept is working out well today.

1642
01:08:05,059 --> 01:08:06,959
It's all about children.

1643
01:08:06,959 --> 01:08:08,359
Not even middle schoolers, just kids.

1644
01:08:09,459 --> 01:08:10,999
If they had been teenagers, we would have won.

1645
01:08:10,999 --> 01:08:12,759
Giving out free cotton candy made a huge difference.

1646
01:08:12,759 --> 01:08:14,129
No, high schoolers would not go there.

1647
01:08:16,469 --> 01:08:18,469
Puppy, walk around carrying the ice cream.

1648
01:08:18,469 --> 01:08:20,169
- Ice cream.
- No, there's no need.

1649
01:08:20,339 --> 01:08:21,609
Just write...

1650
01:08:21,609 --> 01:08:24,139
"handmade gelato ice cream" on the whiteboard.

1651
01:08:24,239 --> 01:08:26,209
No, I'll write it.

1652
01:08:26,509 --> 01:08:27,579
I have pretty handwriting.

1653
01:08:28,209 --> 01:08:29,379
People are looking for ice cream,

1654
01:08:29,479 --> 01:08:31,019
but if you say gelato, they do not recognise it.

1655
01:08:31,019 --> 01:08:32,419
You have to call it gelato ice cream.

1656
01:08:33,719 --> 01:08:37,019
As I observed the place dressed as a puppy,

1657
01:08:37,189 --> 01:08:38,819
I found out that the customers were already full.

1658
01:08:39,219 --> 01:08:40,289
I'm full.

1659
01:08:40,359 --> 01:08:41,489
- Are you full?
- Yes.

1660
01:08:42,329 --> 01:08:43,459
Is there any room left in your stomach?

1661
01:08:44,099 --> 01:08:46,129
- Not really, but I want to eat.
- Are you full?

1662
01:08:46,429 --> 01:08:49,899
So there were a lot of people looking only for desserts.

1663
01:08:49,899 --> 01:08:50,969
(The customers are looking for desserts, feeling full.)

1664
01:08:51,569 --> 01:08:52,969
There's ice cream.

1665
01:08:53,369 --> 01:08:55,469
- Ice cream!
- It's ice cream.

1666
01:08:55,469 --> 01:08:57,169
(Responding to Kim Hoon's signboard)

1667
01:08:57,169 --> 01:08:58,779
- Is that gelato?
- Where?

1668
01:09:00,579 --> 01:09:02,049
How about ice cream churros?

1669
01:09:03,949 --> 01:09:05,749
(We have gelato over there!)

1670
01:09:07,349 --> 01:09:09,519
Since I could not speak, I tried to observe people a lot.

1671
01:09:10,619 --> 01:09:14,059
I thought there would be a high preference for gelato.

1672
01:09:14,129 --> 01:09:16,389
(Handmade gelato ice cream)

1673
01:09:16,389 --> 01:09:18,659
(Crazy Flavour Restaurant)

1674
01:09:18,929 --> 01:09:23,369
(Promoting primarily with ice cream)

1675
01:09:24,839 --> 01:09:26,999
I want to eat this at a restaurant, not at an amusement park.

1676
01:09:27,569 --> 01:09:29,269
- Are you hungry?
- Hello.

1677
01:09:30,779 --> 01:09:32,309
- Are you alone?
- Handmade gelato ice cream?

1678
01:09:32,309 --> 01:09:33,339
(Hiding)

1679
01:09:33,439 --> 01:09:34,549
Which restaurant are you from?

1680
01:09:35,079 --> 01:09:36,079
Where?

1681
01:09:36,079 --> 01:09:37,519
- Over there?
- Crazy flavour Restaurant?

1682
01:09:37,519 --> 01:09:39,119
Lemon yogurt gelato?

1683
01:09:40,889 --> 01:09:42,049
- Okay.
- Okay.

1684
01:09:42,689 --> 01:09:44,189
I want to try the gelato.

1685
01:09:44,459 --> 01:09:46,059
- Me too.
- For dessert.

1686
01:09:46,059 --> 01:09:47,219
(Focusing on the customers who are having a meal)

1687
01:09:47,659 --> 01:09:50,029
But yogurt gelato is a dessert.

1688
01:09:50,029 --> 01:09:51,829
- There is always room for dessert.
- I can eat more.

1689
01:09:52,159 --> 01:09:53,259
I can't eat anymore.

1690
01:09:53,259 --> 01:09:55,769
You should open up the stomach for dessert.

1691
01:09:56,069 --> 01:09:57,169
You can eat dessert.

1692
01:09:58,099 --> 01:09:59,139
This is driving me crazy.

1693
01:09:59,139 --> 01:10:00,139
(Order)

1694
01:10:00,139 --> 01:10:01,309
Now the orders are coming in.

1695
01:10:02,109 --> 01:10:04,709
They say it is super fresh gelato made today.

1696
01:10:05,309 --> 01:10:06,679
I want to eat gelato.

1697
01:10:07,009 --> 01:10:08,149
Ice cream!

1698
01:10:08,149 --> 01:10:10,079
(Kwan Hoon's efforts successfully attract customers.)

1699
01:10:10,679 --> 01:10:12,219
We just need to match the speed.

1700
01:10:13,519 --> 01:10:14,619
It will be ready shortly.

1701
01:10:15,419 --> 01:10:16,519
We have to catch up.

1702
01:10:17,289 --> 01:10:18,619
Please get me one ice cream.

1703
01:10:19,259 --> 01:10:20,259
Okay.

1704
01:10:20,829 --> 01:10:23,529
This is freshly made lemon yogurt ice cream.

1705
01:10:23,629 --> 01:10:25,059
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

1706
01:10:26,159 --> 01:10:27,159
Gelato?

1707
01:10:29,929 --> 01:10:32,469
(Puppy is sneaking over.)

1708
01:10:32,469 --> 01:10:33,739
Puppy!

1709
01:10:33,739 --> 01:10:36,039
(Wandering Panda's ice cream, Kids Restaurant's ice cream)

1710
01:10:36,039 --> 01:10:37,309
Puppy!

1711
01:10:37,809 --> 01:10:41,349
I asked you to do a high-five, but why aren't you doing it?

1712
01:10:42,979 --> 01:10:44,149
The gelato?

1713
01:10:44,449 --> 01:10:46,979
High-five!

1714
01:10:47,519 --> 01:10:49,219
(Puppy is upset.)

1715
01:10:52,419 --> 01:10:54,329
After seeing it work so hard, we should buy the mianbao xia.

1716
01:10:54,989 --> 01:10:56,059
We should do that.

1717
01:10:56,729 --> 01:10:59,299
(They ended up buying Crazy Flavour Restaurant's dish.)

1718
01:10:59,929 --> 01:11:01,699
Even though we have three different ice cream options.

1719
01:11:01,699 --> 01:11:02,699
(Trying the lemon gelato)

1720
01:11:02,699 --> 01:11:04,399
- This is really good.
- Is it?

1721
01:11:04,469 --> 01:11:05,469
It's so delicious.

1722
01:11:06,339 --> 01:11:08,909
(Comparing and analysing the 3 ice cream shops)

1723
01:11:08,909 --> 01:11:10,339
- This is different.
- Right.

1724
01:11:10,409 --> 01:11:12,939
This one is the most delicious among all three ice creams.

1725
01:11:12,939 --> 01:11:13,979
I know, right?

1726
01:11:14,479 --> 01:11:17,349
(Among the ice creams of the three shops,)

1727
01:11:18,519 --> 01:11:21,249
(Crazy Flavour Restaurant takes 1st place.)

1728
01:11:21,919 --> 01:11:23,389
I would have regretted it if I had not tried this.

1729
01:11:24,059 --> 01:11:25,359
The gelato is the most delicious.

1730
01:11:26,819 --> 01:11:28,989
- Let's go.
- Let's go. Let's speed up.

1731
01:11:29,289 --> 01:11:31,059
Hang in there, Puppy.

1732
01:11:34,899 --> 01:11:35,929
I became a mad dog.

1733
01:11:36,899 --> 01:11:39,039
I worked so hard. I think I did really well.

1734
01:11:39,369 --> 01:11:40,499
I felt so proud of myself.

1735
01:11:40,909 --> 01:11:42,169
Nice, just a little bit more.

1736
01:11:43,209 --> 01:11:44,379
I'd be upset if we lost.

1737
01:11:44,379 --> 01:11:46,139
(Crazy Flavour Restaurant has sold 73 plates.)

1738
01:11:46,579 --> 01:11:48,679
Is the booth next door serving just soft ice cream?

1739
01:11:49,249 --> 01:11:50,379
- Yes, it is.
- Yes.

1740
01:11:50,609 --> 01:11:51,819
- If that's the case...
- They can't...

1741
01:11:51,819 --> 01:11:53,019
dispense 50 servings continuously.

1742
01:11:53,019 --> 01:11:54,019
It's impossible.

1743
01:11:54,919 --> 01:11:56,419
Did you get the ice cream ready, Jong In?

1744
01:11:56,889 --> 01:11:58,459
- Not yet.
- Not a single one?

1745
01:11:58,459 --> 01:12:00,389
- No.
- Can you do it for a second?

1746
01:12:00,829 --> 01:12:03,529
About the ice cream... The machine...

1747
01:12:03,929 --> 01:12:05,259
dispenses 5 servings...

1748
01:12:05,259 --> 01:12:07,329
and needs to rest for 15 minutes to get another 5.

1749
01:12:08,299 --> 01:12:10,169
It's an emergency. The ice cream is melting right now.

1750
01:12:10,229 --> 01:12:11,499
Even when dispensed immediately, it melts right away.

1751
01:12:11,839 --> 01:12:14,109
It seems like it can only do up to ten servings at a time.

1752
01:12:14,209 --> 01:12:16,509
- Really?
- We only need to dispense 50.

1753
01:12:16,509 --> 01:12:17,509
Right.

1754
01:12:18,009 --> 01:12:19,709
We have to get them all done during the first half.

1755
01:12:21,449 --> 01:12:23,049
How many do we have now?

1756
01:12:23,379 --> 01:12:24,449
I will head back out again.

1757
01:12:24,879 --> 01:12:26,919
I put on the bear mascot head and took it off to get ice cream.

1758
01:12:26,919 --> 01:12:28,519
So we had some that was done during the first half.

1759
01:12:28,989 --> 01:12:30,249
(Frowning)

1760
01:12:30,419 --> 01:12:32,019
Is there enough ice cream? Do we need more?

1761
01:12:32,159 --> 01:12:34,459
Just get some more if you have spare time.

1762
01:12:34,459 --> 01:12:35,629
We have about 20 servings. Get some more.

1763
01:12:35,629 --> 01:12:36,659
Okay.

1764
01:12:38,329 --> 01:12:39,329
It's so hot.

1765
01:12:42,829 --> 01:12:43,899
Hang in there, Teddy Bear.

1766
01:12:46,569 --> 01:12:48,569
Hoon, go and attract customers.

1767
01:12:48,739 --> 01:12:50,509
- Do what?
- What?

1768
01:12:50,809 --> 01:12:51,909
Drink some water.

1769
01:12:51,909 --> 01:12:54,449
I'll put it in here. I think we have enough.

1770
01:12:55,209 --> 01:12:56,779
Honestly, I was seeing stars.

1771
01:12:56,979 --> 01:12:59,819
I thought I was getting heatstroke.

1772
01:13:01,049 --> 01:13:02,119
This is killing me.

1773
01:13:03,919 --> 01:13:07,059
(Amid the fierce dessert war)

1774
01:13:08,259 --> 01:13:09,759
Okay. Once these go out, we are set.

1775
01:13:10,829 --> 01:13:12,729
We are switching to the second container right away.

1776
01:13:13,259 --> 01:13:15,599
We have to get rid of all these.

1777
01:13:15,599 --> 01:13:17,329
- I'll take them outside.
- Take them outside.

1778
01:13:17,939 --> 01:13:19,339
Chef, I will put the sauces and these items outside.

1779
01:13:19,339 --> 01:13:22,009
Clear everything out. We don't need any of it.

1780
01:13:22,109 --> 01:13:23,709
- I will bring the soda as well.
- Okay.

1781
01:13:24,379 --> 01:13:27,779
(Switching to the second half)

1782
01:13:29,679 --> 01:13:32,979
(Second half: Edward Kwon)

1783
01:13:33,349 --> 01:13:36,519
(Edward Kwon chose the rectangular tray.)

1784
01:13:36,519 --> 01:13:38,289
Before this mission,

1785
01:13:38,759 --> 01:13:42,089
I went to Lotte World once and Everland twice.

1786
01:13:42,659 --> 01:13:45,629
Today, I'm at the amusement park in Yongin...

1787
01:13:45,959 --> 01:13:48,269
where the third mission will take place.

1788
01:13:48,469 --> 01:13:49,929
I noticed...

1789
01:13:50,269 --> 01:13:52,539
there were many food choices available.

1790
01:13:52,639 --> 01:13:54,069
So I thought...

1791
01:13:54,369 --> 01:13:56,709
it'd be a good idea...

1792
01:13:56,709 --> 01:13:58,939
to help people try a bit of everything.

1793
01:13:59,439 --> 01:14:02,379
So it contains the most dishes so far.

1794
01:14:03,049 --> 01:14:05,549
It's the global lunch box...

1795
01:14:05,779 --> 01:14:07,649
with orange cream shrimp and chicken steak.

1796
01:14:07,989 --> 01:14:09,389
(Global lunch box)

1797
01:14:09,389 --> 01:14:11,359
(Shrimp, chicken)

1798
01:14:16,089 --> 01:14:18,759
For the orange cream shrimp...

1799
01:14:19,099 --> 01:14:21,769
It's called the orange zest. It's ground orange skin.

1800
01:14:22,469 --> 01:14:25,869
We're using the orange to give the flavour.

1801
01:14:25,869 --> 01:14:27,139
(Fresh cream sauce on fried shrimp)

1802
01:14:27,369 --> 01:14:31,139
And chicken steak using the peanut glaze.

1803
01:14:31,639 --> 01:14:34,079
I was thinking about Thai-style food.

1804
01:14:34,079 --> 01:14:36,209
Then I decided to use the peanut butter.

1805
01:14:39,319 --> 01:14:40,349
Amazing.

1806
01:14:40,719 --> 01:14:42,819
The chicken looks just perfect.

1807
01:14:42,819 --> 01:14:43,919
(Roasted chicken steak)

1808
01:14:45,659 --> 01:14:47,759
(With the Thai-style peanut glaze sauce)

1809
01:14:50,089 --> 01:14:51,359
(Exclaiming)

1810
01:14:51,359 --> 01:14:52,399
This is good.

1811
01:14:52,829 --> 01:14:54,269
I love the scent of peanut.

1812
01:14:55,269 --> 01:14:57,599
And a lot of visitors pack lunch...

1813
01:14:57,599 --> 01:14:59,799
to Everland.

1814
01:15:00,599 --> 01:15:02,269
So I decided to include fried tofu rice balls.

1815
01:15:03,169 --> 01:15:04,909
(Japanese)

1816
01:15:05,279 --> 01:15:08,609
Then I saw nachos and tacos.

1817
01:15:08,609 --> 01:15:10,079
(Cheese quesadilla, Mexican)

1818
01:15:10,079 --> 01:15:13,379
I decided to add salad...

1819
01:15:13,519 --> 01:15:16,119
to keep the balance and refresh the palate.

1820
01:15:16,119 --> 01:15:17,149
(Tomato pasta salad, western)

1821
01:15:17,289 --> 01:15:21,329
If I include them all in one box,

1822
